From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pocket Arcade contributors <noreply@pocketarcade.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: 47-bit address bounds on Android (ARM64EC)

Madeira bounds two checks at iOS's 39-bit user space. On Linux/Android Wine
maps ntdll, the PE modules and thread stacks near 0x6fff00000000-0x7fff00000000:
- arm64x_check_call sent every call into ntdll to the x64 exit thunk;
- NtDeviceIoControlFile rejected every IO_STATUS_BLOCK on a thread stack with
  STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION (no socket could be created).
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index bf196ab..e5a0d3d 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -1398,7 +1398,9 @@ NTSTATUS SYSCALL_API NtDeviceIoControlFile( HANDLE handle, HANDLE event, PIO_APC
      * one AND. Returning a status keeps the pseudo-process alive and the
      * [iosb-guard] line names the caller so the corruption source can be
      * chased offline. */
-    if (!io || ((ULONG_PTR)io & (sizeof(void *) - 1)) || (ULONG_PTR)io >= 0x8000000000ull)
+    /* Android: user space is 47-bit (Wine puts thread stacks, and so most
+     * IO_STATUS_BLOCKs, near 0x7fff00000000); iOS's was 39-bit. */
+    if (!io || ((ULONG_PTR)io & (sizeof(void *) - 1)) || (ULONG_PTR)io >= 0x800000000000ull)
     {
         static ULONG bogus_n;
         if (bogus_n < 16)
@@ -4968,7 +4970,11 @@ static void __attribute__((naked)) arm64x_check_call(void)
           * Not covered, deliberately, to keep the scope to the observed fault: a
           * NULL or small-but-invalid target still reaches `ldr x16,[x11]` below and
           * faults there, which is what Windows would also do. */
-         "lsr x16, x11, #39\n\t"            /* ml975: beyond 39-bit VA / map coverage? */
+         /* Android: user space and the EcCodeBitMap cover 47 bits, and Wine maps
+          * ntdll and the other PE modules near 0x6fff00000000, far above iOS's
+          * 39-bit limit. With 39 here every call into ntdll took the x64 exit
+          * thunk and started the emulator before it was initialised. */
+         "lsr x16, x11, #47\n\t"            /* beyond user VA / map coverage? */
          "cbnz x16, .Lexit\n\t"             /*        -> not EC code, exit thunk */
          "ldr x16, [x18, #0x60]\n\t"        /* peb -- see above, intentionally x18 */
          "lsr x17, x11, #18\n\t"            /* dest / page_size / 64 */
